# For a bound session, session-start writes the ready mark once, prints the identity and the cheat
# sheet (under 20 lines) at every start (startup, resume, clear, compact); after a compaction it
# also says to re-read the brief and the inbox, prints core's operator and autonomy reload lines and
# the post-compact files a profile listed.
# The identity line carries the derived phase; a second startup leaves the stored phase untouched.
# covers: R-MOD-062, R-HOOK-003, R-HOOK-004, R-HOOK-006, R-HOOK-007, R-HOOK-009, R-BLT-107, R-BLT-108
cd repo
exec ness init --gate true --base main --yes
cp ../ness.toml .ness/ness.toml
store add-session s-aaaaaaaaaaaa root
store add-session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb child-b s-aaaaaaaaaaaa
env NESS_SESSION=s-bbbbbbbbbbbb
env NESS_TEST_NOW=2026-10-08T10:00:00Z
store session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb ready=false
store phase s-bbbbbbbbbbbb waiting-ready
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../startup.txt
! stdout 'After compaction'
! stderr .
store session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb ready=2026-10-08T10:00:00Z phase=waiting-ready
# A second startup keeps the first mark and does not touch the phase (R-HOOK-009).
env NESS_TEST_NOW=2026-10-08T10:05:00Z
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
store session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb ready=2026-10-08T10:00:00Z phase=waiting-ready
# A resume and a clear print the same as a startup, the post-compact list excluded.
stdin ../resume.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../startup.txt
stdin ../clear.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../startup.txt
# After compaction: identity, the re-read line, the cheat sheet, the post-compact list; at most 20 lines.
stdin ../compact.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../compact.txt
! stdout '(?s)(.*\n){21}'
stdout 'Operator communication'
stdout 'Autonomy'
# Rejects: compaction losing the ladder rule (kind line, ness pick, one-rung escalate) or the
# cheat sheet losing ness pick (R-MOD-062).
stdout -count=1 '^- Models: every subagent call carries a `kind: <name>` line and the model and effort `ness pick` gives; the hook refuses a rung above the recommendation unless the prompt has `escalate: <reason>` \(one rung\)\.$'
stdout -count=1 '^  ness pick '
# A root's manager is the operator.
env NESS_SESSION=s-aaaaaaaaaaaa
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
stdout '^ness session s-aaaaaaaaaaaa scope root manager operator size full phase ready$'
stdout -count=1 '^ness cheat sheet$'

-- ness.toml --
ness = "0.1"
project = "p"
base = "main"
gate = "true"
profiles = ["local"]
-- repo/.ness/profiles/local/profile.toml --
name = "local"
[slots]
"ness-entry#post-compact" = { append = "reload.md" }
-- repo/.ness/profiles/local/reload.md --
- docs/sessions/root/plan.md
- docs/sessions/root/decisions.md
-- startup.json --
{"hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"startup","session_id":"c0ffee"}
-- resume.json --
{"hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"resume","session_id":"c0ffee"}
-- clear.json --
{"hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"clear","session_id":"c0ffee"}
-- startup.txt --
ness session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb scope child-b manager s-aaaaaaaaaaaa phase ready
ness cheat sheet
  ness inbox                                       list your open items, one line each
  ness inbox --show ITEM...                        read items in full (--unread: every unread one)
  ness inbox --boundary NOTE [--until T]           state written down; compact me; parked until T
  ness send --to manager|ID|operator --body TEXT|@FILE  [--intent request|fyi|decision|handoff|checkpoint] [--urgent]
  ness reply ITEM --body TEXT|@FILE                [--as resolved|declined|deferred|accepted|returned|withdrawn]
  ness open --scope NAME --tier TIER --brief FILE  launch a child
  ness integrate --subject 'type(scope): summary'  fold this branch through the gate into the manager's
  ness close ID [--note TEXT] [--withdraw] [--authorized WORDS]  close a child; your root, with the operator's words
  ness probe start|run|verdict|stop                probes, when the feature is on
  ness pick --kind NAME                            the model and effort for a subagent
Waiting rule: pull once, then end your turn; the worker wakes you when something arrives.
-- compact.json --
{"hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"compact","session_id":"c0ffee"}
-- compact.txt --
ness session s-bbbbbbbbbbbb scope child-b manager s-aaaaaaaaaaaa phase ready
After compaction: re-read your brief and your inbox first.
ness cheat sheet
  ness inbox                                       list your open items, one line each
  ness inbox --show ITEM...                        read items in full (--unread: every unread one)
  ness inbox --boundary NOTE [--until T]           state written down; compact me; parked until T
  ness send --to manager|ID|operator --body TEXT|@FILE  [--intent request|fyi|decision|handoff|checkpoint] [--urgent]
  ness reply ITEM --body TEXT|@FILE                [--as resolved|declined|deferred|accepted|returned|withdrawn]
  ness open --scope NAME --tier TIER --brief FILE  launch a child
  ness integrate --subject 'type(scope): summary'  fold this branch through the gate into the manager's
  ness close ID [--note TEXT] [--withdraw] [--authorized WORDS]  close a child; your root, with the operator's words
  ness probe start|run|verdict|stop                probes, when the feature is on
  ness pick --kind NAME                            the model and effort for a subagent
Waiting rule: pull once, then end your turn; the worker wakes you when something arrives.
- Operator communication: decision-first and short, long content on a page; the operator reads only your chat, never `ness inbox` and never answers on the phone: write every ask and report in full in the chat, then file it with `ness send --to operator` so the phone points them to you; a child asks only for what its manager cannot settle.
- Autonomy: act at the level your brief states; a root never lowers a child's level; reserved decisions stay the operator's.
- Models: every subagent call carries a `kind: <name>` line and the model and effort `ness pick` gives; the hook refuses a rung above the recommendation unless the prompt has `escalate: <reason>` (one rung).
- docs/sessions/root/plan.md
- docs/sessions/root/decisions.md
